{"type":"message","id":"fa7710c8","parentId":"8fdd8016","timestamp":"2026-06-01T03:33:45.668Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the root endpoint returns \"Unauthorized\" which means the API is up and responding. The POST /send returns 1101 which is a Workers execution error. This is likely a bug in the Cloudflare Workers script - the handler for `/send` is throwing an unhandled exception.\n\nThe 1101 error in Cloudflare Workers means \"Workers execution error\" - essentially the script crashed. This isn't an authentication issue since we're reaching the endpoint.\n\nLet me try to check if there's an alternative endpoint or if maybe the API key format is wrong. But since the cron job instruction mentions `POST /send`, it seems like this endpoint should work...\n\nWait, could this be a rate limiting issue? 1101 is not a standard rate limit error. \n\nLet me explore whether there are other endpoints available that might handle the request differently.","thinkingSignature":"0a0949f4f6f45ed6ec0cd8cc3d2c47b914fd5f52ecaefb0d8dcfde888f61868e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dqq23qdxpsai_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/routes\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dqq23qdxpsai_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 03:30 UTC]\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":13414,"output":330,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27426,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780284818839,"responseId":"066c3093d25b7721cbd33fda70e8b20c"}}
