{"type":"message","id":"408c3bcb","parentId":"e600cc39","timestamp":"2026-06-01T03:33:58.657Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the response is HTTP 500 with body \"error code: 1101\". The Cloudflare Workers script for `/send` is throwing an internal error. This is a server-side issue with the Workers script, not something I can fix from the client side.\n\nLet me check the GET /history endpoint works fine, but POST /send consistently fails with 500/1101. This seems like a bug in the Workers script that handles the send endpoint.\n\nI should report this in my response - the platform is reachable, the heartbeat status can be read, but the send endpoint has a bug (HTTP 500). Let me also check if there's maybe a different way to post - perhaps via query parameters on GET, or another endpoint.\n\nLet me try GET /send or other variants.","thinkingSignature":"19ded617176fd20caea4bfca3086acbe29d5d7812e1b1f3503b18abb2a452e24"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ib6c7nel2vr0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+test\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ib6c7nel2vr0_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/post\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":14408,"output":293,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28383,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780284832201,"responseId":"066c30a096758e96bea4fc7d7f1c70f3"}}
